---
import ChessBoard from "../components/ChessBoard.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Spacer from "../components/Spacer.astro";

const STRENGTHS = [
  { label: "Fast (0.3s a move)", value: 300 },
  { label: "Normal (1s a move)", value: 1000 },
  { label: "Slow (3s a move)", value: 3000 },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Play Oxid'"
  description="Play a game against Oxid', my 2700 Elo chess engine written in Rust, compiled to WebAssembly and running in your browser."
>
  <h1>Play Oxid'</h1>
  <p>
    Oxid&apos; is the chess engine I have been writing in Rust from near scratch, and this is it running in your
    browser: the same search and the same neural network as the native build, compiled to WebAssembly. Nothing is sent
    to a server, so the engine is thinking on your machine, in a background thread, at whatever speed your laptop
    manages.
  </p>
  <p>
    The engine and its network weigh about 2.4MB, so nothing downloads until you pick a colour below. I wrote the
    story of building it in <a href="/blog/series/building-a-chess-engine-in-rust">a series of posts</a>, and the
    source lives on <a href="https://github.com/Blightwidow/oxide-chess-engine" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
  </p>
  <Spacer units={1} />
  <div class="game" data-chess>
    <div class="panel">
      <p class="status" data-status role="status" aria-live="polite">
        Choose a colour to start.
      </p>
      <div
        class="progress"
        data-progress
        role="progressbar"
        aria-label="Loading the engine"
        aria-valuemin="0"
        aria-valuemax="100"
        hidden
      >
        <span class="progress-bar" data-progress-bar></span>
        <span class="progress-text" data-progress-text></span>
      </div>
      <div class="controls">
        <button type="button" data-start="white">Play as white</button>
        <button type="button" data-start="black">Play as black</button>
      </div>
      <label class="strength">
        Thinking time
        <select data-strength>
          {
            STRENGTHS.map((strength) => (
              <option value={strength.value} selected={strength.value === 1000}>
                {strength.label}
              </option>
            ))
          }
        </select>
      </label>
      <button type="button" data-takeback disabled>Take back a move</button>
    </div>
    <div class="board-column">
      <ChessBoard />
      <div class="promotion" data-promotion hidden>
        <span class="promotion-label">Promote to</span>
        {
          ["q", "r", "b", "n"].map((piece) => (
            <button type="button" class="promotion-choice" data-promote={piece} />
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
    <ol class="moves" data-moves aria-label="Moves played"></ol>
  </div>
  <Spacer units={1} />
  <p class="footnote">
    Moves are shown the way the engine speaks them, from square to square. The browser build is single-threaded and
    has no opening book or endgame tablebases, so it plays a little below the 2700 Elo the native build is rated at.
  </p>
</Layout>

<script>
  import { startChessGame } from "../scripts/chess-game";

  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-chess]");

  if (root !== null) {
    startChessGame(root);
  }
</script>

<style>
  .game {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .board-column {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .panel {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .status {
    margin: 0;
    flex: 1 1 100%;
    min-height: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .controls {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  button,
  select {
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: inherit;
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--foreground-rgb), 0.4);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.7rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  button:hover:not(:disabled),
  select:hover {
    border-color: rgba(var(--foreground-rgb), 0.9);
  }

  button:disabled {
    opacity: 0.45;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }

  .strength {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .progress {
    flex: 1 1 100%;
    position: relative;
    height: 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--foreground-rgb), 0.4);
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .progress-bar {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    width: 0;
    background: rgba(var(--foreground-rgb), 0.25);
    transition: width 0.2s linear;
  }

  .progress-text {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .moves {
    list-style: decimal inside;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.5rem;
    max-height: 8rem;
    overflow-y: auto;
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--foreground-rgb), 0.2);
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .moves:empty {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Sits over the board, where the promoting pawn is about to land. */
  .promotion {
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline-start: 50%;
    inset-block-start: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    background: rgb(var(--background-rgb));
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--foreground-rgb), 0.5);
    border-radius: 6px;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
  }

  .promotion[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .promotion-label {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .promotion-choice {
    display: flex;
    width: 2.4rem;
    height: 2.4rem;
    padding: 0.15rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .promotion-choice :global(svg) {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  .promotion-choice :global(svg) {
    stroke-width: 1.4;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
    paint-order: stroke fill;
  }

  .promotion-choice[data-color="white"] :global(svg) {
    fill: #f4f4ef;
    stroke: #14161a;
  }

  .promotion-choice[data-color="black"] :global(svg) {
    fill: #16181c;
    stroke: #e8e8e2;
  }

  .footnote {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  @media (min-width: 700px) {
    .moves {
      columns: 2;
    }
  }
</style>
